Subject: [PATCH 43/76] v2 transport fixes round 5 (Astra R5-1, R5-2): fatal
 helper labels errors only by identity with trusted built-in exception types
 and never invokes exception-controlled descriptors or formatting, exact-type
 diagnostic fields; READY status type checked before comparison with only
 READY/FAILURE accepted; bounded startup-response writer (oversized
 READY/FAILURE become a small FAILURE); PLE identity validation shared before
 every breakable-runner initialization incl. the profiling path (Sol draft,
 Fable applied/tested)

Tests: tests/v1/ple_offload 62/62; new test_round5_transport.py 13/13.
